(7486357, 1191451, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>A very appealing image that contributes well to the challenge<br/> <br/>A lovely well controlled exposure that goes to the limit of both boundaries yet still retains detail, well done Janine. As for the mono conversion well, its equally well controlled and hugely appealing with a full range of tones. Great composition, everything contributes well to the end result. Good timing with lovely motion blur of the mans hand as he raises the food to his mouth. I love the tiled walls and the simple yet poignant statement of the graffiti without which the image would be poorer yet still easily recognisable as continental. A lovely job.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club A very appealing image that contributes well to the challenge A lovely well controlled exposure that goes to the limit of both boundaries yet still retains detail, well done Janine. As for the mono conversion well, its equally well controlled and hugely appealing with a full range of tones. Great composition, everything contributes well to the end result. Good timing with lovely motion blur of the mans hand as he raises the food to his mouth. I love the tiled walls and the simple yet poignant statement of the graffiti without which the image would be poorer yet still easily recognisable as continental. A lovely job.', '2016-12-08 05:20:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(7486358, 1191433, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>A very appealing image that contributes well to the challenge<br/> <br/>Another unique image Eugene. I love the sharp focus where its needed and the soft focus wingtips which, as you say, suggests a little motion blur, it works well. The angle is lovely giving a further sense of dynamic action. I can understand why you will have removed the background given the rest of the probably chaotic scene that would have been behind it. The plain white background you have gone with makes the image unique leaving us to focus entirely on the lovely detail of the bird itself so that we can appreciate the sheer beauty of these gorgeous little birds. Shame the blue and white was minimal editing...!</td>', 'Hello from the critique club A very appealing image that contributes well to the challenge Another unique image Eugene. I love the sharp focus where its needed and the soft focus wingtips which, as you say, suggests a little motion blur, it works well. The angle is lovely giving a further sense of dynamic action. I can understand why you will have removed the background given the rest of the probably chaotic scene that would have been behind it. The plain white background you have gone with makes the image unique leaving us to focus entirely on the lovely detail of the bird itself so that we can appreciate the sheer beauty of these gorgeous little birds. Shame the blue and white was minimal editing...!', '2016-12-08 05:28:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(7486359, 1191232, 102315, '<td valign="top">I''m happy with the top 10 in a FS but am disappointed at the same time. I was holding a 6.5 the entire time and the day before rollover dropped to a 6.4 then woke up to a 6.3. <br/> <br/>Oh well</td>', 'I''m happy with the top 10 in a FS but am disappointed at the same time. I was holding a 6.5 the entire time and the day before rollover dropped to a 6.4 then woke up to a 6.3.  Oh well', '2016-12-08 06:14:08.000000', NULL, 0),
